{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 53, :comments ["<b>Blessed</b> — The meaning is that the poet saw through holy spirit the coming of the messiah; therefore he gave thanks to HaShem. Others say: like the way of Job, for the discerning one blesses HaShem even though the enemy reviles him — he bears his disgrace. And a great Spanish sage says: that the scribe who first wrote this book wrote at the end of the book 'Blessed be HaShem who helped us write it all,' the way of scribes in our generation to write at the end 'Blessed is He who gives strength to the weary.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 89, :notes {0 "The closing quotation appears to be a formulaic phrase rather than a direct biblical citation; rendered as a liturgical formula."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:43.162701233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}